{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nA completion close always dispatches the billable verifier after deterministic guards, even when the ticket already carries a cryptographically certified `completion-verifier` PASS bound to the exact immutable commit being closed. The existing signature verifier can authenticate the stored completion op-cert, but the close seam never consults it. A runtime probe created a certified same-ref completion record on an in-progress bug, then closed at that exact SHA: the provider spy was called once.\n\nThe earlier standalone `verify-completion` command returns a signable result but does not persist an attestation. Changing that command into a mutating producer is out of scope; reuse applies only when a genuine ticket-contained completion attestation already exists (for example, from the trusted op-cert producer). The closed Locust task concerns bounded retry of insufficiency-only FAILs and is not a duplicate.\n\n## Proven root cause\n`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py::_completion_precheck` unconditionally calls `close_autoresume.verify_with_auto_resume` after its deterministic guards. `verify_with_auto_resume` immediately invokes `llm.verify_completion`; neither seam checks the ticket's existing `completion-verifier` attestation. The required verifier, SHA pin, and material fingerprint are already available from the signature and plan-material infrastructure.\n\n## Repair plan\n- Add a fail-safe reuse check at the close auto-resume seam before provider dispatch.\n- Resolve the close target ref once and require the stored completion op-cert to certify cryptographically.\n- Require an authenticated `completion-verifier: PASS` manifest.\n- Require the authenticated `verified-at-sha` to equal the resolved close target SHA.\n- Require the authenticated material fingerprint to equal the ticket's current material fingerprint.\n- Reject attestations invalidated by a later reopen.\n- Return a close-compatible reused PASS result so the normal close, durable verdict, and post-close signing path remain unchanged.\n- Fall through to the existing verifier for every absent, malformed, unverifiable, stale, differently pinned, or otherwise ineligible record.\n\n## Test contract card\n- authoritative_contract: operator-approved same-ref attested-PASS reuse requirement on this ticket.\n- trigger_preconditions: ticket is in progress; completion gate enabled; a completion-verifier op-cert is already stored; explicit --ref resolves to the op-cert SHA.\n- production_path: transition -> close precheck -> close autoresume/reuse seam -> locked close -> completion signing.\n- observable_postcondition: provider call count is zero and the ticket closes signed.\n- negative_controls: different SHA, invalid signature, missing pin, stale material, and pre-reopen attestation each call the provider exactly once.\n- test_tier: lifecycle integration over an ephemeral git repo and real ticket store, with only the provider replaced by a spy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A close at the exact SHA of a valid stored completion PASS makes zero completion-provider calls.\n- [ ] A reused PASS still produces a signed closed ticket.\n- [ ] A reused PASS leaves durable completion evidence for the closed ticket.\n- [ ] A changed resolved ref forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] A cryptographically invalid completion record forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] A non-PASS or wrong-kind record forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] An attestation without an authenticated SHA pin forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] An attestation without an authenticated material fingerprint forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] A material fingerprint mismatch forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] An attestation invalidated by a later reopen forces a fresh completion verification.\n- [ ] Explicit CLI `--ref` reaches the reuse decision through the normal lifecycle path.\n- [ ] Focused tests pass.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787082769888386001,"uuid":"9bafcd64-d1c6-449d-a60b-125e6821f925"}